---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../../config/site';
import { localizedPath } from '../../i18n/utils';
import { t } from '../../i18n/ui';

const locale = 'en' as const;
const strings = t(locale);
---

<Legal
  locale={locale}
  routeKey="privacy"
  title={strings.meta.privacyTitle}
  description={strings.meta.privacyDescription}
>
  <p>
    At {site.legalName} (“{site.shortName}”, “we”) we respect your privacy. This Privacy Policy
    explains what personal data we process, for what purpose and under what conditions, as well as
    the rights available to you.
  </p>
  <p>
    This Policy is governed by <strong>Law No. 29733, the Personal Data Protection Law</strong> of
    Peru and by its Regulations, approved by <strong>Supreme Decree No. 016-2024-JUS</strong>, in
    force since 30 March 2025.
  </p>

  <h2 id="controller">1. Owner of the personal data bank</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Legal name:</strong> {site.legalName}</li>
    <li><strong>Tax ID (RUC):</strong> {site.taxId}</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Registered address:</strong> {site.address.street}, {site.address.district},{' '}
      {site.address.city}, {site.address.country}
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Privacy contact:</strong>{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email.privacy}`}>{site.email.privacy}</a>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="data">2. Personal data we process</h2>

  <h3>2.1 Data you provide</h3>
  <p>
    This Site <strong>contains no data collection forms</strong>. Contact takes place by email or
    through the channels listed in the contact section. When you write to us, we process the data
    you choose to include in your message, typically:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>First name and surname.</li>
    <li>Email address and, where applicable, telephone number.</li>
    <li>The company or entity you represent and your role.</li>
    <li>The content of your message and any information you voluntarily include in it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>2.2 Browsing data</h3>
  <p>
    The Site is static and <strong>does not use cookies, tracking pixels, advertising or analytics
    tools</strong> that build profiles of its visitors.
  </p>
  <p>
    However, our hosting provider automatically logs technical data inherent to the operation of the
    internet — IP address, date and time of the request, browser type and requested page — for the
    sole purpose of delivering the content, maintaining service security and preventing abuse. We do
    not link those logs to identified individuals or use them for commercial purposes.
  </p>

  <h3>2.3 Sensitive data and minors</h3>
  <p>
    We do not request sensitive data as defined by Law No. 29733. Please do not include such
    information in your communications unless it is strictly necessary and has been agreed in
    advance.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Site is aimed at professionals and organisations, not minors, and we do not knowingly
    collect their data. If we become aware that we have processed a minor’s data without the
    appropriate authorisation, we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="purposes">3. Purposes of processing</h2>
  <p>We process your personal data solely to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Handle and respond to enquiries, information requests and proposals you send us.</li>
    <li>Prepare and send quotations or service proposals when you request them.</li>
    <li>Manage pre-contractual and contractual relationships with clients, suppliers and partners.</li>
    <li>Comply with applicable legal, accounting and tax obligations.</li>
    <li>Ensure the security and proper functioning of the Site.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>We do not use your data to send unsolicited marketing communications</strong>, to build
    profiles, or to make automated decisions producing legal effects concerning you.
  </p>

  <h2 id="lawfulness">4. Lawful basis</h2>
  <p>Processing is based, depending on the case, on:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Your free, prior, express, informed and unequivocal consent</strong>, given when you
      voluntarily send us a communication.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Performance of a contract or pre-contractual measures</strong> taken at your request.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Compliance with legal obligations</strong> to which we are subject.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Where the basis is consent, you may withdraw it at any time by writing to{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email.privacy}`}>{site.email.privacy}</a>, without affecting the
    lawfulness of processing carried out before the withdrawal.
  </p>

  <h2 id="retention">5. Retention period</h2>
  <p>We keep data for as long as necessary to fulfil the purpose for which it was collected:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Enquiries that do not lead to a commercial relationship:</strong> up to twelve (12)
      months from the last contact.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Clients and suppliers:</strong> for the duration of the relationship and thereafter
      for the applicable legal, accounting and tax limitation periods in Peru.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Once those periods have elapsed, data is securely and irreversibly deleted or anonymised.
  </p>

  <h2 id="recipients">6. Recipients and processors</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell, transfer or trade your personal data. Only providers acting as processors on our
    behalf may access it, bound by contract and by confidentiality and security obligations:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Website hosting:</strong> GitHub, Inc. (GitHub Pages).</li>
    <li><strong>Email and productivity:</strong> Microsoft Corporation (Microsoft 365).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We may also disclose data to administrative or judicial authorities where legally required to do
    so.
  </p>

  <h2 id="transfers">7. Cross-border data flows</h2>
  <p>
    The providers listed above may host or process information on servers located outside Peru,
    mainly in the United States of America and the European Union. This constitutes a cross-border
    flow of personal data under Law No. 29733 and its Regulations.
  </p>
  <p>
    In such cases we require our providers to offer contractual guarantees of an adequate level of
    protection, equivalent to that provided by Peruvian law, through data protection contractual
    clauses and security and confidentiality commitments.
  </p>

  <h2 id="security">8. Security measures</h2>
  <p>
    We apply technical, organisational and legal measures to protect personal data against
    unauthorised processing, loss, alteration or improper access. These include:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Encryption of Site traffic using HTTPS/TLS.</li>
    <li>Multi-factor authentication and access control on a least-privilege basis.</li>
    <li>Logging and periodic review of access to information.</li>
    <li>Confidentiality agreements with staff and providers.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    No system is completely infallible. Should a security incident affecting your personal data
    occur, we will notify the National Authority for Personal Data Protection{' '}
    <strong>within forty-eight (48) hours</strong> of becoming aware of it and, where applicable,
    inform you, in accordance with the Regulations in force.
  </p>

  <h2 id="rights">9. Your rights (ARCO)</h2>
  <p>As the data subject, you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Access:</strong> find out what data of yours we process, its origin, purpose and to
      whom it is disclosed.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Rectification:</strong> correct inaccurate, incomplete or outdated data.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cancellation:</strong> request deletion of your data where the purpose has been
      fulfilled, the processing period has expired or you withdraw consent.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Objection:</strong> object to processing where it causes you harm or a legitimate
      ground applies.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You may additionally exercise the rights to <strong>information</strong>,{' '}
    <strong>portability</strong> and <strong>withdrawal of consent</strong> recognised by the
    Regulations in force.
  </p>

  <h3>How to exercise them</h3>
  <p>
    Send a request to <a href={`mailto:${site.email.privacy}`}>{site.email.privacy}</a>, or to our
    address in section 1, enclosing:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>Your full name and a copy of your identity document.</li>
    <li>The right you wish to exercise and a clear description of your request.</li>
    <li>An address or email where we can send our reply.</li>
    <li>Any supporting documents, where applicable.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    We will reply within a maximum of <strong>twenty (20) days</strong> for the right of access and{' '}
    <strong>ten (10) days</strong> for the rights of rectification, cancellation and objection,
    counted from receipt of the request. Exercising these rights is free of charge.
  </p>

  <h2 id="complaint">10. Complaints to the authority</h2>
  <p>
    If you believe your request was not handled properly or that your rights have been infringed,
    you may lodge a complaint with the <strong>National Authority for Personal Data Protection
    (ANPD)</strong> of the Peruvian Ministry of Justice and Human Rights, via{' '}
    <a href="https://www.gob.pe/autoridad-nacional-de-proteccion-de-datos-personales" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
      gob.pe/autoridad-nacional-de-proteccion-de-datos-personales
    </a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">11. Changes to this Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Policy to reflect regulatory changes or changes in our processes. The version
    in force is always the one published on this page, showing its last updated date. If a change is
    substantial and affects the processing of your data, we will communicate it through the
    available contact channels.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">12. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    For any question about this Policy or about the processing of your personal data, write to{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email.privacy}`}>{site.email.privacy}</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    See also our <a href={localizedPath('terms', locale)}>Terms of Service</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
